}

\section{Streamable HTTP}{

\code{transport = "http"} serves the streamable HTTP transport with
httpuv: \code{POST /mcp} carries one JSON-RPC message (or a batch) and
answers with \code{application/json}; \code{GET /mcp} answers 405 because this
server never pushes messages; \code{DELETE /mcp} ends a session;
\code{GET /health} reports the server and the tidybrreg version. When the
\code{MCP_BEARER_TOKEN} environment variable (or \code{token}) is set, every
\verb{/mcp} request must carry it as \code{Authorization: Bearer}.
}

